# CLAUDE.md — local operational truth for `multilanetesting`
#
# This file is gitignored. Copy it to CLAUDE.md and fill in the values for your
# specific system under test. Never commit real hosts, partitions, or secrets.
#
# Instructions:
#   cp CLAUDE.md.example CLAUDE.md
#   # fill in the sections that apply to your target system
#   # leave sections blank or remove them if that surface does not exist

## System under test

<!-- Replace with your system name and a one-line description -->
System: <system name>
Description: <what it does>

## Surfaces and lanes

<!-- Tick the lanes that apply. This comes from your Phase 0 surface inventory memo. -->
- [ ] Web / DOM — URL: `<MULTILANE_WEB_BASE_URL>`
- [ ] API contract — host: `<MULTILANE_TARGET_HOST>`
- [ ] WS contract — endpoint: `<MULTILANE_WS_URL>`
- [ ] Screen driver — VNC/RDP host: `<SCREEN_TARGET_HOST>`, partition: `<SCREEN_RPS_PARTITION>`

## Known blockers

<!-- Anything confirmed unobservable or blocked. Mirror into docs/memory/blocker-index.md. -->
- None yet

## Test partitions (screen-driver lane)

<!-- Which partitions are available and safe to use? -->
- `TEST_A` — available: yes/no
- `TEST_B` — available: yes/no
- `TEST_C` — available: yes/no
- `PROD` — **NEVER target this**

